public import Theory.Representation.ReeF4.BinaryDegree.ExceptionalTensor.Classification.Steinberg.FiniteRootAction.RootCurves.Algebraic

/-!
# Genuine Ree root curves for the finite restriction argument

For every geometrically short native root in either chamber and every finite
field parameter, an element of the actual Ree fixed group contains that root
factor, with all other factors strictly higher in the additive degree
`(2,2,1,1)`. The original factor order is preserved. The algebraic and action
endpoints use the literal coefficient embedding, without any root-generation,
classification, or finite-irreducibility premise.

Source: GLS3 Table 2.4 and Theorem 2.8.2; Steinberg (1963), Section 12.
-/
